# gradlew has to actually be executable on Linux CI, and this repo is
# developed on Windows, where NTFS has no concept of the Unix execute bit —
# `git add` on Windows silently stores it as mode 644. `text eol=lf` also
# pins the line endings so a Windows checkout can never reintroduce CRLF into
# a POSIX shell script's shebang line. Without this, the fix applied once in
# history (`git update-index --chmod=+x`) is one Windows-side re-add away
# from silently reverting.
gradlew text eol=lf
